{"id": "EUVD-2026-76278", "enisaUuid": "58a68cf6-d1c7-3d15-bb82-7d7f3f4294e1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-pcache: fix use-after-free and invalid seg operations in kset_replay()\n\nIn kset_replay, when key->seg_gen is stale (key->seg_gen <\nkey->cache_pos.cache_seg->gen), cache_key_put(key) is called but then\nkey->cache_pos.cache_seg is accessed as the argument to cache_seg_get().\nThis is a use-after-free on the freed key memory. Although mempool\nrecycled memory is not immediately reclaimed or overwritten in practice,\nthis is still a potential UAF bug.\n\nAdditionally, for expired invalid keys, setting the cache->seg_map bit\nand calling cache_seg_get() is unreasonable since the corresponding\nsegment data is no longer valid.\n\nFix both issues by moving cache_seg_get() and __set_bit() after the\ngen check, so they only execute for valid keys, and using continue to\nskip invalid keys.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:39", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1894fc7a3bab90143dcd26ef8ee27040ef4a7501", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f39a3e9cc5946473e16d6f5071b2ee0216c56d06", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c2e894eac398b258f12fdec73ed6ba081047f7b3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vjx8-9mvv-9939", "CVE-2026-80955"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1365e4e9-8639-3110-8b9a-1c3416f7aa70", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <c2e894eac398b258f12fdec73ed6ba081047f7b3"}, {"id": "145e04e3-695d-3889-aff4-f070347d656d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "5a449436-6a85-366d-b1d2-961c30e0a736", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5ee8b4a2-1c10-36d1-a916-d94fc39089a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "691431b5-7764-3fe1-942f-7914d160f123", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <1894fc7a3bab90143dcd26ef8ee27040ef4a7501"}, {"id": "b0c926ef-c488-3fc8-9e31-53718e477bb8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "d0c7995e-4039-3186-8019-94fcf1047480", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <f39a3e9cc5946473e16d6f5071b2ee0216c56d06"}, {"id": "eeeb62cf-c583-3328-94ff-81f72cd2eaa3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e7a9b8ca-a75d-35c6-a288-54ab7e6234b9", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}